# Documentation requirements by type — mandatory

## Exposed tables (`BaseTable` descendants)
For every Exposed table object/class that inherits from `BaseTable`, type-level KDoc must include:
- `Schema is created by a Flyway migration in \`db/migration/<module>/<feature>/\`.`
- `The app must include this path in its Flyway migration locations.`

## Public API (interfaces)
- Class-level KDoc: role/purpose.
- Each method: purpose + `@param` + `@return`.

## Implementation classes (classes implementing interfaces)
- **Mandatory class-level KDoc** explaining concrete behavior (how it delegates, where it runs, caching, background persistence, logging, etc.).
- Do not duplicate interface method docs on overrides.

## Dagger modules (`@Module`)
- Every module must have class-level KDoc describing what it provides/binds.
- Aggregate modules must list included submodules.

## Error models (sealed error hierarchies)
- Class-level KDoc: purpose; `[publicArgs]` are for client/localization, `[secretArgs]` for logs.
- Each variant: short description + `@param` for ctor params; state whether each param goes to `[publicArgs]` or `[secretArgs]` and whether it is used in localized messages.

## Value classes / enums / data classes
- Class/enum-level KDoc: purpose and usage.
- Value classes: `@param` for the wrapped value; KDoc for public methods + companion functions.
- Enums: one line per entry describing when to use it.

### Value class API (mandatory)
For every `@JvmInline value class` that wraps an identifier or parseable type, provide:
1) `asHexDashString()` instance method (canonical hex-with-dashes)
2) `generate()` companion function
3) In the same file, two `String` extensions:
   - `toXxxOrNull()` (parse, return null if invalid)
   - `toXxxOrThrow()` (parse, throw if invalid)

## Holders / config objects (e.g. `*ConfigHolder`)
- Object-level KDoc must explain **why** the holder exists (decoupled from DI, runtime reconfiguration, defaults).
- Briefly document `set`/`get` behavior (e.g. default when never set).

## Localized / user-facing strings
- Keep messages concise; avoid generic filler.
- Use only `[publicArgs]` placeholders in templates; never expose `[secretArgs]` to clients.
